cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnyDisasterMapping, please cite this repository, and the upstream benchmark paper it builds on (see references)."
title: "AnyDisasterMapping - extended"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmed
    given-names: Syed Rafi
version: "v5.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SyedRafiAhmedGIS/AnyDisasterMapping"
abstract: "A unified PyTorch codebase for Earth-observation disaster mapping: 24 registered benchmark datasets across 13 disaster domains (segmentation, change detection, semantic change detection), 34 model implementations, one-command smoke tests, an ONNX export path, and a 17-notebook Colab collection sharing a single tested core. Extended distribution built on the AnyDisaster benchmark codebase released with the reference below."
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Earth Observation for Disaster Mapping: Benchmarks, Methods, Challenges and Future Perspectives"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.2139/ssrn.6725082"
    url: "https://ssrn.com/abstract=6725082"
